  "apparatus": "Shared Stuttgart 400 kg ball-screw / linear direct-drive table, 0.72 m travel. The README explicitly refers to the magnetic force compensation from 10.18419/darus-2563. In the author thesis, Appendix A.3 identifies Heidenhain LS187C table linear scale, separate AM2048S/R motor encoder and four Kistler 9323A sensors. Treat as repeated studies on one rig.",
  "shared_bench_identity": "File bytes SHA-256 plus complete native x_meas_table array serialized as contiguous little-endian float64, one digest per MATLAB acquisition. All six pairwise comparisons among darus-2563/3109/3003/3152 have zero exact content matches on both tests. Partial subsequences, rerendered runs and related settings are outside this equality test.",
  "methods": [
    "Used channel-specific MATLAB dSPACE XIndex and nearest timestamps on the first nominal 1 kHz grid; rejected any row with a required or present optional channel farther than 0.1251 ms. Retained points coincide exactly with source timestamps. Inverter torque comes from the drive; table position is a separate encoder signal.",
    "Scanned all 99 MAT acquisitions for enable-to-disable transitions and nonzero lastError. For the 22 constant-speed files, required planned and measured table speed each within 5% of nominal, in each signed direction. For the 12 motor-sine force runs, retained measured motion amplitude, including full-interval shutdown effects where present.",
    "Cross-release comparison uses the two 25 mm/s full-stroke runs from this release (compensation active per README and verified nonzero drive command) and the corresponding uncompensated files from darus-2563. For each direction, restrict to 0.02 ≤ planned position < 0.70 m and planned speed within 1%. Compute median nut force and table following error for each 10 mm bin; remove the median of the 68 force bins separately in each run to reduce sensitivity to constant force-sensor drift."
  ],
  "results": [
    "99 numeric files give 1,436,052 synchronized rows with separate motor/table positions, motor request/inverter torque and measured nut load; 188 command-grid rows were excluded for absent coincident signals.",
    "44 directional cruise summaries cover 1–750 mm/s. For 200 N nominal motor-sine input, the range of measured table travel is 16.64–24.87 µm across 0.1, 0.5 and 1 Hz; for 300 N it is 193.68–859.47 µm. At 340 N it ranges from 0.367 to 9.842 mm; one of these runs experienced shutdown.",
    "Three sine records include an observed sigEnable 1→0: F340_1_0Hz at 19.27475 s (error 3), F400_0_1Hz at 9.53865 s and F500_0_1Hz at 3.66896 s (error 1). In both error-1 cases the error code clears during the disabled interval.",
    "At 25 mm/s on the same rig, the spatially centered RMS nut-force-bin medians are 53.08/13.41 N backward and 53.37/13.43 N forward (uncompensated/compensated). Corresponding RMS of the 68 bin medians of table position error is 7.687/1.029 µm and 7.890/1.027 µm."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Motor-sine amplitude encoded in a filename is the nominal axial excitation; the force sensor at the nut and the inverter’s torque estimate are separate quantities. Numerical error codes have no release-specific decoder here. Observed disabling is not proof of current saturation.",
    "Shared apparatus, different acquisition sessions and four physical traversals; compensation comparison cannot separate all tuning, thermal or sensor-drift effects. Spatial-bin metrics are not all-sample RMS."
  ],
